    {
      "id": "5opvvlz",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "UNITS AND MEASUREMENTS"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "A physical quantity is defined by a numerical magnitude and a standard unit (Q = n × u).",
        "The SI system consists of 7 fundamental base quantities: Mass (kg), Length (m), Time (s), Temperature (K), Electric Current (A), Luminous Intensity (cd), and Amount of Substance (mol).",
        "Supplementary units include the Radian for plane angle and Steradian for solid angle.",
        "Dimensional formulas express derived physical quantities in terms of base dimensions [M], [L], and [T].",
        "Measurement errors are broadly categorized into systematic errors, random errors, and gross errors."
      ],
      "id": "z3j7uj2"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
