    {
      "id": "o93gnqg",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "MCQs"
    },
    {
      "id": "ucwhjqc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Q1."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3gc786d",
      "content": "A train is moving with a speed of 72 km/h. Its speed in m/s is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "byr9650",
      "content": "A) 18 m/s"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "m3qepje",
      "content": "B) 20 m/s"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "15vys1t",
      "content": "C) 22 m/s"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "1mht86z",
      "content": "D) 25 m/s"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "o29juxm",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: B (20 m/s)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "m9ghkvm",
      "content": "Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4mgixnk",
      "content": "Step 1: Understand the unit conversion."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wgzbegp",
      "content": "1 kilometre (km) = 1000 metres (m)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sbh0ejk",
      "content": "1 hour (h) = 3600 seconds (s)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k3c8nhy",
      "content": "Step 2: Convert 1 km/h into m/s"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qniwk6c",
      "content": "1 km/h = 1000 m / 3600 s"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1ctzfck",
      "content": "= 5/18 m/s (standard conversion factor)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "svwlcqp",
      "content": "Step 3: Convert 72 km/h"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "q27w4ba",
      "content": "72 × (5/18)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "zwxbtci",
      "content": "Step 4: Simplify mathematically"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "6a16a4w",
      "content": "72 ÷ 18 = 4"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ph7je3b",
      "content": "4 × 5 = 20"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "1bul98j",
      "content": "Final Answer = 20 m/s"
    },
    {
      "id": "fuowk16",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Q2."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gkptg4f",
      "content": "The density of a substance having mass 6 kg and volume 3 m³ is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "i2rijmp",
      "content": "A) 1 kg/m³"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "qktn9ta",
      "content": "B) 2 kg/m³"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "s9ypdlx",
      "content": "C) 3 kg/m³"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ysm7hky",
      "content": "D) 18 kg/m³"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "2j5xhqp",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: B (2 kg/m³)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cnyug8c",
      "content": "Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3af1dae",
      "content": "Step 1: Write the formula of density."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qx3wrgh",
      "content": "Density (ρ) = Mass / Volume"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8dfkxev",
      "content": "Step 2: Substitute given values."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "91kbfuo",
      "content": "Mass = 6 kg"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "af0ieok",
      "content": "Volume = 3 m³"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "a1wuoeu",
      "content": "ρ = 6 / 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zjzue7q",
      "content": "Step 3: Divide."
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Base Quantities",
        "Derived Quantities"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Independent of any other physical quantity.",
          "Defined and derived from base quantities."
        ],
        [
          "Limited to 7 fundamental quantities in the SI system.",
          "Unlimited in number as new quantities are defined."
        ],
        [
          "Examples: Mass (kg), Length (m), Time (s).",
          "Examples: Force (N), Pressure (Pa), Velocity (m/s)."
        ]
      ],
      "id": "6tj0loe"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "eqhpsti",
      "content": "ρ = 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0224q4v",
      "content": "Unit check: kg ÷ m³ = kg/m³"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wrmuluh",
      "content": "Final Answer = 2 kg per cubic metre"
    },
    {
      "id": "3vi7wr3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Q3."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sdayikl",
      "content": "A force acts on a 5 kg body producing acceleration of 3 m/s². The force is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "9ldys3n",
      "content": "A) 8 N"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "z3hbygs",
      "content": "B) 10 N"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "2f9ihoz",
      "content": "C) 15 N"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "m1t2me4",
      "content": "D) 20 N"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "o5jtvkk",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: C (15 N)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "b8u3gde",
      "content": "Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3gk49o4",
      "content": "Step 1: Use Newton’s Second Law of Motion."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jot21z8",
      "content": "Force (F) = Mass (m) × Acceleration (a)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k07iyyh",
      "content": "Step 2: Substitute values."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "nz8t5sv",
      "content": "m = 5 kg"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "eiuuizm",
      "content": "a = 3 m/s²"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "umxazqk",
      "content": "F = 5 × 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ckr9l82",
      "content": "Step 3: Multiply."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "2yqujt5",
      "content": "F = 15"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g8tghu5",
      "content": "Unit Explanation:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ym9d08r",
      "content": "kg × m/s² = Newton (N)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "gdgg0iy",
      "content": "Final Answer = 15 N"
    },
    {
      "id": "ght8l2b",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Q4."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dp69k80",
      "content": "A force of 12 N moves a body through 4 m. The work done is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "1b7dmgh",
      "content": "A) 3 J"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "stdx3tr",
      "content": "B) 16 J"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "q1j9iom",
      "content": "C) 48 J"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "6lr3787",
      "content": "D) 8 J"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "qnclcb2",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: C (48 J)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1i3m77o",
      "content": "Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ohl9nyy",
      "content": "Step 1: Write formula of work."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jicw3cd",
      "content": "Work (W) = Force (F) × Displacement (s)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "o8gkt23",
      "content": "Step 2: Substitute values."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "q0xigoo",
      "content": "F = 12 N"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "06w3376",
      "content": "s = 4 m"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "nicbi6h",
      "content": "W = 12 × 4"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Light year and Parsec are units of distance, not time. (1 Parsec = 3.26 Light Years = 3.08 × 10¹⁶ m).",
        "High-frequency dimensional formulas: Gravitational Constant G = [M⁻¹L³T⁻²], Planck's Constant h = [ML²T⁻¹], and Pressure P = [ML⁻¹T⁻²].",
        "Least count of standard measuring instruments: Vernier Caliper (0.1 mm or 0.01 cm), Screw Gauge (0.01 mm)."
      ],
      "id": "3pj1gta"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mhoq8uf",
      "content": "Step 3: Multiply."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "hcvrnt2",
      "content": "W = 48"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a5wa6cz",
      "content": "Unit Explanation:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dfevwjf",
      "content": "Newton × metre = Joule (J)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "8o15jf1",
      "content": "Final Answer = 48 J"
    },
    {
      "id": "qiuswvk",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Q5."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qev25da",
      "content": "If pitch of a screw gauge is 0.5 mm and circular scale has 50 divisions, its least count is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ntjs1gc",
      "content": "A) 0.01 mm"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "qjohoj0",
      "content": "B) 0.02 mm"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "b4xyc9m",
      "content": "C) 0.1 mm"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "zvlxzq5",
      "content": "D) 0.001 mm"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "age36dz",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: A (0.01 mm)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sgxmh2t",
      "content": "Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k15fxs5",
      "content": "Step 1: Write formula of Least Count."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lx5vptr",
      "content": "Least Count (LC) = Pitch / Number of circular scale divisions"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f0g8ox5",
      "content": "Step 2: Substitute given values."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "kmcz08z",
      "content": "Pitch = 0.5 mm"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "l1qnhvb",
      "content": "Divisions = 50"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "lskijuo",
      "content": "LC = 0.5 / 50"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hzd2ygr",
      "content": "Step 3: Perform division carefully."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "db5pqve",
      "content": "0.5 ÷ 50 = 0.01"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "kudpztl",
      "content": "Unit remains millimetre (mm)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "lgcbthf",
      "content": "Final Answer = 0.01 mm"
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}